# VideoGeneratorApp — daily batch schedule (UTC).
#
# Crontab environment does NOT expand $HOME; the lines below rely on the
# `HOME` variable cron sets for your user. Install with `crontab -e`.
#
# The pipeline contract is:
#   python -m src.pipeline --category <ai_tech|finance|health_fitness|general_knowledge>
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Category rotation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The batch should cover one of the four categories per day (4-day rotation):
#   ai_tech -> finance -> health_fitness -> general_knowledge -> (repeat)
#
# Easiest option: use a small rotation script that picks the category from the
# day of year and shells out to the pipeline, then cron calls that script:
#
#   30 2 * * * cd "$HOME/VideoGeneratorApp" && .venv/bin/python deploy/oracle/rotate.py >> "$HOME/videogen.log" 2>&1
#
# If you prefer to stay cron-only, use FOUR staggered lines — one per category,
# each firing every 4 days on a different weekday (01:00 UTC = 06:30 IST),
# so exactly one category runs per day:
#
#   30 2 * * 0 cd "$HOME/VideoGeneratorApp" && .venv/bin/python -m src.pipeline --category ai_tech       >> "$HOME/videogen.log" 2>&1
#   30 2 * * 1 cd "$HOME/VideoGeneratorApp" && .venv/bin/python -m src.pipeline --category finance        >> "$HOME/videogen.log" 2>&1
#   30 2 * * 2 cd "$HOME/VideoGeneratorApp" && .venv/bin/python -m src.pipeline --category health_fitness >> "$HOME/videogen.log" 2>&1
#   30 2 * * 3 cd "$HOME/VideoGeneratorApp" && .venv/bin/python -m src.pipeline --category general_knowledge        >> "$HOME/videogen.log" 2>&1
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Single-line example (fixed category) — adjust the category as needed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
30 2 * * * cd "$HOME/VideoGeneratorApp" && .venv/bin/python -m src.pipeline --category ai_tech >> "$HOME/videogen.log" 2>&1
